From: Kotesh Murugan <koteshlost@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] interactivetx: handle NULL from psbt_append_output

Follow-up to 0002. With the assert removed, psbt_append_output can now
return NULL when libwally rejects the insert. The interactive-tx loop
must surface that as a protocol error string instead of dereferencing
NULL.

---
 common/interactivetx.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/common/interactivetx.c b/common/interactivetx.c
--- a/common/interactivetx.c
+++ b/common/interactivetx.c
@@ -742,6 +742,8 @@ char *process_interactivetx_updates(const tal_t *ctx,
 			out = psbt_append_output(ictx->current_psbt,
 						 scriptpubkey,
 						 amt);
+			if (!out)
+				return tal_fmt(ctx, "Output rejected by PSBT");

 			psbt_output_set_serial_id(ictx->current_psbt,
 						  out,
